{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2040","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Ordered Permutations"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider a permutation$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ $$$p_1, p_2, \\ldots, p_n$$$ of integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. We can introduce the following sum for it$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$S(p) = \\sum_{1 \\le l \\le r \\le n} \\min(p_l, p_{l + 1}, \\ldots, p_r)$$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let us consider all permutations of length $$$n$$$ with the maximum possible value of $$$S(p)$$$. Output the $$$k$$$-th of them in lexicographical$$$^{\\text{‡}}$$$order, or report that there are less than $$$k$$$ of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$A permutation of length $$$n$$$ is an array consisting of $$$n$$$ distinct integers from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in arbitrary order. For example, $$$[2,3,1,5,4]$$$ is a permutation, but $$$[1,2,2]$$$ is not a permutation ($$$2$$$ appears twice in the array), and $$$[1,3,4]$$$ is also not a permutation ($$$n=3$$$ but there is $$$4$$$ in the array). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{†}}$$$For example: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For the permutation $$$[1, 2, 3]$$$ the value of $$$S(p)$$$ is equal to $$$\\min(1) + \\min(1, 2) + \\min(1, 2, 3) + \\min(2) + \\min(2, 3) + \\min(3) =$$$ $$$1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 3 = 10$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For the permutation $$$[2, 4, 1, 3]$$$ the value of $$$S(p)$$$ is equal to $$$\\min(2) + \\min(2, 4) + \\min(2, 4, 1) + \\min(2, 4, 1, 3) \\ +$$$ $$$ \\min(4) + \\min(4, 1) + \\min(4, 1, 3) \\ +$$$ $$$\\min(1) + \\min(1, 3) \\ +$$$ $$$\\min(3) =$$$ $$$2 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 4 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 3 = 17$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{‡}}$$$An array $$$a$$$ is lexicographically smaller than an array $$$b$$$ if and only if one of the following holds: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a$$$ is a prefix of $$$b$$$, but $$$a \\ne b$$$; or "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" in the first position where $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ differ, the array $$$a$$$ has a smaller element than the corresponding element in $$$b$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$; $$$1 \\le k \\le 10^{12}$$$) — the length of the permutation and the index number of the desired permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10 ^ 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, if there are less than $$$k$$$ suitable permutations, print $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise, print the $$$k$$$-th suitable permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n3 2\n3 3\n4 11\n4 6\n6 39\n7 34\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 3 2 \n2 3 1 \n-1\n2 4 3 1 \n-1\n2 3 4 5 7 6 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let us calculate the required sum for all permutations of length $$$3$$$ (ordered lexicographically):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Permutation"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Value of $$$S(p)$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[1, 2, 3]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$10$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[1, 3, 2]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$10$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[2, 1, 3]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$9$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[2, 3, 1]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$10$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[3, 1, 2]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$9$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[3, 2, 1]$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$10$$$"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, you have to print the second suitable permutation of length $$$3$$$. Looking at the table, we see that it is the permutation $$$[1, 3, 2]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, you have to print the third suitable permutation of length $$$3$$$. Looking at the table, we see that it is the permutation $$$[2, 3, 1]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2040C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2040/problem/C"}